# Redis Iris basics: settings.
#
# Copy this file to .env next to iris_basics.py and uncomment what you have. marimo loads
# it automatically. To reuse another project's file instead, set IRIS_BASICS_ENV_FILE to
# its path. A value already present in your environment wins over any file.
#
# Comments must stay on their own lines: loaders disagree about an inline "# note", and
# some keep it as part of the value.
# Each column asks only for its own settings. Without them it shows a "not configured"
# note (column 2 also has a data-model cell that works offline).
# The console is https://cloud.redis.io

# ---- Column 0 · Redis Search (also the database Context Retriever loads into) ----
# Console: Databases > your database > Configuration > Public endpoint gives host and
# port. Security > Default user > eye icon shows the password.
# No database yet? A free 30 MB one is enough: https://redis.io/try-free/
# The free tier has no TLS, so the scheme is redis:// and not rediss://.
# Give either the one-line URL ...
# REDIS_URL=redis://default:<password>@<host>:<port>
# ... or the parts below, which are used only when REDIS_URL is unset.
# REDIS_HOST=
# REDIS_PORT=
# REDIS_USERNAME=default
# REDIS_PASSWORD=
# REDIS_SSL=false
# REDIS_DB=0

# ---- Column 1 · LangCache ----
# Console: LangCache > your service > Configuration > Connectivity lists the URL, the
# Cache ID and, when the service is first created, the API key. The key is shown once.
# Use a cache of your own for this notebook. Never press Generate key on a shared cache:
# it kills the key everyone else is using.
# LANGCACHE_HOST=https://<region>.langcache.redis.io
# LANGCACHE_CACHE_ID=
# LANGCACHE_API_KEY=
# Optional. The name of an attribute that was defined on the cache when it was created
# (Configuration > Attributes). Leave it unset if the cache has none.
# LANGCACHE_SCOPE_ATTR=

# ---- Column 2 · Context Retriever ----
# Console: Context Retriever > Admin keys > New admin key. It is shown once, and the tab
# needs an existing Context Retriever service. This column also needs the REDIS_URL above,
# on a database the hosted service can reach, with Search and JSON.
# CTX_ADMIN_KEY=
# Optional. Only for a self-managed install or a different region; the defaults suit
# Redis Cloud.
# CTX_API_URL=
# CTX_MCP_URL=

# ---- Column 3 · Agent Memory ----
# Console: Agent Memory > your service > Configuration > General settings shows the
# Endpoint (include https://) and the Store ID. API keys tab > New API key makes a key,
# shown once.
# MEMORY_API_BASE_URL=https://<endpoint>
# MEMORY_STORE_ID=
# MEMORY_API_KEY=
